        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nJOHN J. SAMSON, ESQ., Assistant Attorney General, Olympia, Wash; on behalf of Petitioner.\nMICHAEL R. DREEBEN, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting Petitioner.\nSUZANNE LEE ELLIOTT, ESQ., Hartford, Conn; on behalf of Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in 06-413, Uttecht versus Brown."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit's conclusion that Mr. Brown is entitled to habeas corpus relief should be reversed for three reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Counsel, may I ask you one thing, which I have assumed, and I think it is correct, but I'd like to be sure of it. Is it the case, is it correct, that prior to the voir dire questions, no one had given a statement to the venire people of what the law was with respect to the imposition of the death penalty; is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit found that the State courts made no Finding of fact and, as Mr. Brown has essentially admitted in his response brief, there are two State court findings of fact, one by the Washington Supreme Court and one by the trial judge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0000-0008",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF MICHAEL R. DREEBEN ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES AS AMICUS CURIAE SUPPORTING THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: You may reserve the remainder of your time for rebuttal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Does that respond to the possible suggestion that Judge Kozinski made that what he really did was act on the basis of no objection, rather than on the basis of a finding that he failed to make?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Prosecution",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There were 12 objections by the prosecution to various jurors that they should be excused for cause because of inability to apply the law as Washington gives it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, what is -- I know, Justice Breyer; just on this point. The defense actually volunteered \"no objection.\" MR. DREEBEN: Said \"We have no objection.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What has this to do with the -- aside from the explanation, when I read through the transcript, as I have, it seemed to me in the transcript he didn't say a word that suggested he's against giving the death penalty."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Why -- why was there no objection if this was so clear?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You think he could have imposed the death penalty in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Elliott",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under Washington law, I think there would be a sufficient basis for excusing juror Deal if he said I now know what the statutory scheme is, and only if there's some possibility for release of Mr. Brown and the opportunity for him to kill again, would I impose the death penalty."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cbde50418314-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There were actually 12, I think. Weren't there 12 objections by the prosecution?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-06-413",
